# Git identity

This is a personal open-source project. Every commit must use only this identity:

- Author and committer: `3136321049 <3136321049@users.noreply.github.com>`
- Any `Co-authored-by` trailer must use exactly `3136321049 <3136321049@users.noreply.github.com>`.

Before committing, run `git config user.name` and `git config user.email`; if they differ, set them to the values above for this repository. Never add an author, committer or co-author line with any other personal or employer email address.

# Keep work context out of the repo

Do not write any of the following into files, commit messages, PR titles or PR descriptions:

- Employer names, internal domains, intranet URLs, internal IP addresses or hostnames
- Local machine paths that contain a username (for example `/Users/<name>/...`)
- Passwords, API keys, tokens, cookies or SSH keys

If such content is found in the repo, stop and tell the user instead of committing it.
